## Accessibility Implementation Patterns

### Form Error Handling
Based on successful implementations, use these patterns for accessible forms:

```typescript
// Input component with error support
<Input
  id="email"
  type="email"
  error={errors.email}
  helpText="We'll never share your email"
  aria-invalid={!!errors.email}
  aria-describedby={errors.email ? 'email-error' : 'email-help'}
/>

{errors.email && (
  <div id="email-error" role="alert" className="text-destructive text-sm mt-1">
    {errors.email}
  </div>
)}
```

### Skip Navigation Links
Always include skip-to-main-content links on all pages:

```typescript
<a
  href="#main-content"
  className="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-50 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:bg-primary focus:text-primary-foreground focus:rounded-md"
>
  Skip to main content
</a>
```

### ARIA Live Regions
Use ARIA live regions for dynamic content updates:

```typescript
// Polite announcements (status updates)
<div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" className="sr-only">
  {statusMessage}
</div>

// Assertive announcements (errors)
<div aria-live="assertive" aria-atomic="true" className="sr-only">
  {errorMessage}
</div>

// Loading states
<button aria-busy={isLoading} aria-live="polite">
  {isLoading ? 'Loading...' : 'Submit'}
</button>
```

### Password Input with Visibility Toggle
Implement accessible password inputs:

```typescript
<button
  type="button"
  onClick={toggleVisibility}
  aria-label={isVisible ? 'Hide password' : 'Show password'}
  className="absolute right-2 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2"
>
  {isVisible ? <EyeOff /> : <Eye />}
</button>
```

### Mobile Navigation
Implement accessible mobile navigation:

```typescript
<button
  aria-label="Toggle navigation menu"
  aria-expanded={isOpen}
  aria-controls="mobile-nav"
  onClick={toggleMenu}
>
  <Menu />
</button>

<nav
  id="mobile-nav"
  aria-label="Main navigation"
  className={cn(isOpen ? 'block' : 'hidden')}
>
  {/* Navigation items */}
</nav>
```

### Toast Notifications
Implement accessible toast notifications:

```typescript
<div
  role="alert"
  aria-live="polite"
  aria-atomic="true"
  className="toast toast-success"
>
  {message}
</div>
```

### Color Contrast Requirements
- **Normal text**: Minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio
- **Large text** (18pt+ or 14pt+ bold): Minimum 3:1 contrast ratio
- **UI components**: Minimum 3:1 contrast ratio
- Test with tools like WebAIM Contrast Checker or axe DevTools

### Screen Reader Utilities
Use `.sr-only` class for screen reader-only content:

```css
.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  padding: 0;
  margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border-width: 0;
}

.sr-only:focus {
  position: static;
  width: auto;
  height: auto;
  padding: inherit;
  margin: inherit;
  overflow: visible;
  clip: auto;
  white-space: normal;
}
```

